projects.description:
This project develops an open-source, diffusion-based super-resolution (SR) pipeline for enhancing the resolution of gravitational lensing images. High-resolution lensing data is often limited, and the project also aims to create a synthetic benchmark dataset of paired LSST-like low-resolution and Roman-like high-resolution images.

The developed pipeline will be compared against state-of-the-art SR approaches, with an analysis of their respective strengths and limitations. This project lays the groundwork for future applications of SR in downstream tasks such as classification and regression of lens properties.

Deliverables include:

- a synthetic benchmark dataset of paired low- and high-resolution gravitational lensing images;

- a diffusion-based pipeline for SR;

- comparative analysis of SR techniques on the benchmark dataset;

 - open-source code base and final report.
